<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37939" root="لكث" body-key="l">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكَثَ</span></b> , [aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكُثَ</span></b> ,] inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكْثٌ</span> (and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لِكَاثٌ</span>, IAar),
<i>He struck,</i> or <i>smote;</i> (K;) accord. to IAar, who
does not particularize the hand, nor the foot:
(TA:) or, <i>with his hand,</i> or <i>his foot,</i> accord. to
some: (TA:) or, <i>with</i> [perhaps a mistake for
<i>upon</i>] <i>the mouth.</i> (Kr.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لكد</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكَتَهُ</span>,
[aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكُثَ</span></b> ,] <i>He overburdened him.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكِثَ</span>,
aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكَثَ</span></b> , [inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكَثٌ</span>,] <i>He</i> (a camel) <i>was affected
with the disorder called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكَثٌ</span>, or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُكَاثٌ</span>. (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكِثَ بِهِ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكَثَ</span></b> , <i>It</i> (dirt [see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكْثٌ</span>]) <i>adhered to it;</i>
(K;) i. e., to the vessel. (TA.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكِدَ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَكِعَ</span>.]

